## 2) 047-deprecate-skill-benchmark → 003/006 (`deprecate-skill-benchmark`, seq 70)

### 2.1 Timeline row

`| 70 | \`deprecate-skill-benchmark\` | 2026-09-11T17:07:53Z | 2026-09-11T19:53:21+02:00 | \`system-deep-loop/047-deprecate-skill-benchmark\` (merged 2026-09-20) | complete | confirmed |`

### 2.2 Status

**Complete — fully evidenced.**

- `spec.md:37` — `**Status** | Complete`; `graph-metadata.json:42` — `"status": "complete"`; `implementation-summary.md:24` — `completion_pct: 100`, `implementation-summary.md:42` — Completed 2026-09-11.
- `acceptance-criteria.md:57-63` — all seven rows `Met` with evidence; `acceptance-criteria.md:88` — `Closeable: Yes`.
- **No contradiction** across `spec.md`, `acceptance-criteria.md` and `graph-metadata.json`.

### 2.3 Changelog block

> `047-deprecate-skill-benchmark` removed the `skill-benchmark` lane from every reachable surface — five runtime command trees, the hub registry and router pair, the advisor command-bridge projection, its script and fixture trees, and three runtime ledger libraries — so the `system-deep-loop` hub registers five workflow modes where it registered six (`spec.md:23`, `implementation-summary.md:51`, `acceptance-criteria.md:58`). 196 tracked files were deleted and 57 edited, while the 554 historical benchmark reports other skills own were preserved byte-identical (`implementation-summary.md:51`, `acceptance-criteria.md:60`). It mattered because every surface that still advertised the lane was a route to code that should not run (`spec.md:23`), and it closed with residue deliberately left as operator questions rather than silent fixes: a dead `'skill-benchmark'` string constant, four `sk-doc` scripts that imported the deleted tree, a fleet-wide manual-playbook runner gone with the lane, and retrieval corpora that still index the vocabulary (`implementation-summary.md:139-141`, `implementation-summary.md:143`, `spec.md:223-225`).

### 2.4 At-a-glance bullet

- **The sixth lane removed, not renamed** — `skill-benchmark` is gone from every reachable surface and the hub registers exactly five workflow modes (`spec.md:23`, `acceptance-criteria.md:58`), with the 554 historical reports other skills own untouched (`acceptance-criteria.md:60`) and the residue recorded as operator questions rather than fixed on this packet's authority (`spec.md:223-225`).

### 2.5 Before-and-after addendum

- **A lane removed cleanly.** `047-deprecate-skill-benchmark` took the `skill-benchmark` lane out of five runtime command trees, the hub registry and router, the advisor bridge, its script and fixture trees and three runtime ledger libraries, so the hub now registers five workflow modes instead of six (`spec.md:23`, `implementation-summary.md:51`). It deleted 196 tracked files and edited 57 while keeping the 554 historical benchmark reports owned by other skills byte-identical (`implementation-summary.md:51`, `acceptance-criteria.md:60`), and it left its residue — a dead type constant, four broken `sk-doc` imports, a missing manual-playbook runner, indexed vocabulary — as recorded operator questions (`implementation-summary.md:139-141`, `implementation-summary.md:143`).

### 2.6 Parent phase-map row (`003-mode-contracts-migration-and-cutover`)

`| 6 | \`006-deprecate-skill-benchmark\` | complete | predecessor \`005-synthesis-chat-presentation\`; successor \`none\` |`

### 2.7 Contradictions / exceptions

None internal. The open questions and limitations are recorded, not contradictory (`spec.md:223-225`, `implementation-summary.md:139-144`).

