## 3) 048-fanout-convergence-mode-flag → 002/008 (`fanout-convergence-mode-flag`, seq 71)

### 3.1 Timeline row

`| 71 | \`fanout-convergence-mode-flag\` | 2026-09-11T20:55:35.915Z | 2026-09-11T22:55:50+02:00 | \`system-deep-loop/048-fanout-convergence-mode-flag\` (merged 2026-09-20) | complete | confirmed |`

### 3.2 Status

**Complete — evidenced.**

- `spec.md:41` — `**Status** | Complete`; `implementation-summary.md:41` — Status Complete; `graph-metadata.json:36` — `"status": "complete"`.
- No `acceptance-criteria.md` exists: the packet is Level 1 (`spec.md:29`), which scaffold-for-skips AC — expected, not a defect.
- Verification rows PASS at `implementation-summary.md:101-104` (runner syntax, unknown-value rejection with `INPUT_VALIDATION`, accepted value, all three emission points).
- **No contradiction** across documents.

### 3.3 Changelog block

> `048-fanout-convergence-mode-flag` fixed a flag that was documented and reached nothing. The command surface documented `--convergence-mode` with four values, but the fan-out runner never read it, so every lineage took the default while the caller believed otherwise — a completed run recorded `convergenceMode: "standard"` and `maxIterations: 6` against a caller that had asked for `off` and `5` (`implementation-summary.md:55-57`, `spec.md:51`). The runner now validates the value and carries it into the leaf's prompt config, command line and setup bindings, an unknown value fails fast with the valid list, and an absent flag changes nothing (`spec.md:90-92`, `implementation-summary.md:102-104`). It mattered because the gap was invisible: the carried `--stop-policy=max-iterations` produced the same visible outcome, so only the recorded config revealed the divergence (`implementation-summary.md:58-59`).

### 3.4 At-a-glance bullet

- **A documented flag that finally arrives** — The fan-out runner now reads and validates `--convergence-mode`, threads it to the leaf's prompt config, command line and setup bindings, and rejects unknown values instead of falling back to the default that produced the original silence (`spec.md:90-92`, `implementation-summary.md:102-104`).

### 3.5 Before-and-after addendum

- **A silent fan-out default made visible.** `048-fanout-convergence-mode-flag` found that `--convergence-mode` was documented with four values but the fan-out runner never read it, so a lineage ran `standard` against a caller who asked for `off` — invisible because the carried `--stop-policy=max-iterations` produced the same visible outcome (`implementation-summary.md:55-59`). The runner now validates the value and threads it to the leaf at all three emission points, and an unknown value fails with an input error instead of slipping through (`spec.md:90`, `implementation-summary.md:102-104`).

### 3.6 Parent phase-map rows (`002-substrate-and-orchestration`)

Amend existing row 7 (`002/spec.md:49`): successor `none` → `008-fanout-convergence-mode-flag`:

`| 7 | \`007-convergence-termination-and-health\` | in_progress | predecessor \`006-novelty-claims-continuity-and-projections\`; successor \`008-fanout-convergence-mode-flag\` |`

Append:

`| 8 | \`008-fanout-convergence-mode-flag\` | complete | predecessor \`007-convergence-termination-and-health\`; successor \`009-spec-protocol-ledger-events\` |`

### 3.7 Contradictions / exceptions

None. Known limitations are recorded honestly: the leaf's per-mode handling is unchanged and untested here, and pre-change runs recorded the default regardless of caller intent (`implementation-summary.md:110-116`).

