## 4) 049-deep-loop-alignment-review → 006/013 (`deep-loop-alignment-review`, seq 72)

### 4.1 Timeline row

`| 72 | \`deep-loop-alignment-review\` | 2026-09-15T09:48:33Z | 2026-09-15T11:50:15+02:00 | \`system-deep-loop/049-deep-loop-alignment-review\` (merged 2026-09-20) | complete | confirmed |`

Evidence-column caveat: `complete` is evidenced by `spec.md:50`, `goal.md:75-80` and all 17 children; `graph-metadata.json:55` alone reads `in_progress`. If the orchestrator treats graph metadata as the status authority, this row becomes `in_progress` / `disputed` — I recommend against that (see 4.2/4.7).

### 4.2 Status

**Complete — evidenced by the packet's own primary documents; one contradicted derived field.**

- `spec.md:50` — `**Status** | Complete`; phase map rows 1-17 all `Complete` at `spec.md:103-120`; `goal.md:75-80` — all six completion criteria checked `[x]`.
- No `implementation-summary.md` and no `acceptance-criteria.md`: phase parent by design (its phase children own plan/tasks/summary; the content-discipline note is at `spec.md:20-28`).
- **Contradiction:** `graph-metadata.json:55` — `"status": "in_progress"`, disagreeing with `spec.md:50` and with all 17 children's own `Status: Complete` rows (e.g. `001-angle-driven-review/spec.md:36`, `017-guard-index-and-parent-doc-fixes/spec.md:25`). Evidence favors `complete`; the derived field appears stale (last save 2026-09-16, while the phase map and goal record the final state).
- **Merge-relevant staleness:** `spec.md:55-56` carries `Predecessor | 048-fanout-convergence-mode-flag` and `Successor | None` from its former top-level lineage; once nested under 006 those fields no longer describe its adjacency (048 lands under 002). Flag for reconciliation; not a status contradiction.

### 4.3 Changelog block

> `049-deep-loop-alignment-review` read the whole deep-loop system as one architecture and made its surfaces agree. Twenty angle-driven review iterations ran in two waves across four lanes on DeepSeek V4.1 Flash max and GLM 5.3 Flash max, with wave-two angles rewritten from wave-one findings (`spec.md:78`), and every confirmed finding at any severity became its own phase (`spec.md:69`). Seventeen phases closed the rosters, version authority, leaf manifests and doctrine reachability, catalog and README truth, confirm-variant parity, ledger stems, agent mirrors, containment and severity language, and routing doctrine and discovery, plus two operator-added phases for the iteration-record contract and the drift guard, trigger index and parent-document defects (`spec.md:103-120`). It mattered because nobody had read the system as one architecture or against the repo rules that say how it should have been built (`spec.md:66`); the parent closes with all six completion criteria checked (`goal.md:75-80`).

### 4.4 At-a-glance bullet

- **The whole system read as one architecture** — A twenty-iteration angle-driven review across four lanes turned every confirmed finding of any severity into its own phase, and seventeen phases then aligned rosters, version authority, leaf manifests and doctrine reachability, catalogs and READMEs, confirm variants, ledger stems, agent mirrors, containment language and routing doctrine, ending with the goal's criteria checked (`spec.md:69`, `spec.md:103-120`, `goal.md:75-80`).

### 4.5 Before-and-after addendum

- **A review that ended in agreement, not findings.** `049-deep-loop-alignment-review` ran twenty angle-driven review iterations in two waves across four lanes (`spec.md:78`) and never stopped at the report: every confirmed finding at any tier became its own phase — seventeen in all — fixing the surfaces the earlier containment work left disagreeing, through rosters, version authority, leaf manifests and doctrine reachability, catalog and README truth, confirm-variant parity, ledger stems, agent mirrors, containment and severity language, routing doctrine, and two operator-added closeout phases (`spec.md:66`, `spec.md:103-120`). It lands Complete on all six completion criteria, while its own `graph-metadata.json` still reads `in_progress` — a stale derived field the orchestrator should reconcile (`goal.md:75-80`, `graph-metadata.json:55`).

### 4.6 Parent phase-map row (`006-runtime-docs-and-integrity-hardening`)

`| 13 | \`013-deep-loop-alignment-review\` | complete | predecessor \`012-deep-loop-test-debt\`; successor \`none\` |`

(Row 12 stays reserved for the sibling lane's `012-deep-loop-test-debt`.)

### 4.7 Contradictions / exceptions

